docs(process): note the at-quote commit template is PowerShell-only; Bash uses -F (process/P3)

Applies the bash-tool-commit-heredoc backlog entry's cheap proposal. The commit
guidance is a PowerShell single-quoted here-string, but the ship-loop commits
through the Bash tool (worktree commits need a literal -C path). In git-bash that
here-string is not a here-string — the subject silently becomes a bare at-sign,
caught only on a %s readback (an amend round-trip).

- process-rules.md: added a note after the worktree literal-path commit rule that
  from Bash the body is passed via -F - heredoc or -F tempfile; the PowerShell
  here-string template is PowerShell-only.
- Marked the backlog entry Status: applied (archival to applied.md follows in the
  post-#1782 straggler round, to avoid an applied.md conflict).

Pure-docs; agent-size + is-pure-docs gates clean.

